    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by **Trea Turner** (81.27) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), both of whom project as elite starts against favorable matchups. **Trea Turner** draws a premium spot atop the order against Lauer, benefiting from a high-run-environment projection and the exact speed profile we prioritize to capture stolen bases in this 5x5 format. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** finds himself in an ideal situation; his dynamic platoon advantage (14%) against Montero, K, combined with his leadoff role, makes him a primary target for counting stats. **Kyle Schwarber** (79.42) and **Yordan Alvarez** (75.00) provide the necessary thump in the middle of the order, with **Yordan Alvarez** carrying an elite xwOBA of 0.480 that transcends even moderate park factor concerns.\n\nWe are leveraging significant platoon edges to optimize our lineup, specifically with **Colt Keith** (65.43) and **Christian Yelich** (65.41), both of whom see double-digit efficiency boosts from favorable handedness matchups. **Junior Caminero** (66.77) remains a high-floor play despite a tougher matchup against Fisher, as his consistent plate discipline and strong xwOBA keep him locked in the lineup. The most difficult bench decision involved **Chase Meidroth** (42.55), who was squeezed out of the utility slot by **Carson Benge** (43.90). While **Chase Meidroth** offers utility, his projected efficiency drop due to the opposing SP skill of Alexander, T tipped the scales toward **Carson Benge**, whose platoon edge provided just enough marginal value to clear our start threshold.\n\nManagers should monitor the wind conditions for **Dillon Dingler** (49.39), **Colt Keith**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, as a \"Wind In\" advisory is currently suppressing their base scores by 5%. While **Dillon Dingler** sits near the edge of our starting range, we are maintaining him in the lineup due to the depth of the catcher position and his favorable order placement. Elsewhere, we continue to stash **Hyeseong Kim**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Lars Nootbaar** as they remain off the active roster, alongside minor leaguers like **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, who do not factor into today\u2019s tactical rotation. Outside of the wind risk, the primary danger remains the moderate SP skill of Henderson, R against **Carson Benge**, but we are comfortable with the volume of high-efficiency starts across the rest of the board.",
